A||||7||Austin||Flat floor conversion.||||1||
Z||000000||Austin||09-17-2001||03:48 PM||||What is all needed to do a flat floor conversion in a Fiero?  I know u have to get a smaller gas tank or something like that.  I'm sure it would make many Ferrari kits look way better on the interior.  It would also be cool just to have it done on a Fiero.  Somebody should offer a flat floor conversion as a service.||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroFanaticus2||09-17-2001||04:33 PM||||Design it and create it and you'll be the only one I know of.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||09-17-2001||04:42 PM||||The one thing I would caution you on is that by removing some of the tunnel and making it flat, you've just removed a major portion of the strength of the body. You would probably need to reinforce the floor similar to a convertible. But even then, You would be transferring any major shock load (like potholes) to the "A" pillars and roof structure. The results could be cracked fiberglass and/or windshields.<P><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif"> ||||reg||4
Z||000003||Austin||09-17-2001||10:18 PM||||I guess I will have to fill up all the potholes in town then.||||reg||6
Z||000004||rogergarrison||09-18-2001||12:07 AM||||It def will weaken the structure. and you wouldnt have a gas tank, unless you mounted an aftermarket one somewhere else (not a good idea)||||reg||1
Z||000005||artherd||09-18-2001||03:15 AM||||It's a very non-trivial re-desighing of the entire superstructure of the Fiero...<P>Would be kinda cool, but where *would* you put the gas tank ? ;()<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroJoe||09-18-2001||10:29 AM||||The gas tank is already in the safest part of the car, and it also adds a good center "ballast" wieght when full, which helps with the Fiero's F/R weight ratio.  For example, if you added a fuel cell in the trunk area (only other place you could), when it was full your car would be tail heavy and handling characteristics would be changed.<P>Even on newer FWD unibody cars there is still somewhat of a tunnel, becuase it acts as a big rail to support most of the car.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||KissMySSFiero||09-18-2001||02:01 PM||||rodney Dickman had a good idea in his mera(saw it at the GTO show in Chicago)  he got rid of the glove box and made the consol just go back to the firewall.  looked awesome.  but was actually a little higher than the stock console because the comp was now under where you elbow sits.  however it didnt look higher, he just told  me it was.  A++++ mod there.  <P><BR>the only reason i see doing it would be for ummmmmmm....you know your GF doesnt want to reach over the hump....but then again thats why you would get a cadi..=Þ<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||12
